Next: make a token for each service with `assistant service key <name>` (it's printed once; put it in the service's own environment file, readable only by you), and point the service at http://127.0.0.1:8790 (or the "service_notify" "port" in config.json). A Python client to copy in is addons/service-notify/client/multiclaude_service.py.
A press guards against a model deciding the owner meant yes, not against an assistant set on forging one (they run as the same Linux user): see "How far a button can be trusted" in the README.
